    <statement><p>Let <m>F(3) = 1, F'(3) = 2, H(3) = 5, H'(3) = 4</m>.</p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>If <m>G(z) = F(z)\cdot H(z)</m>, then <m>G'(3) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If <m>G(w) = F(w)/H(w)</m>, then <m>G'(3) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1\cdot 4+2\cdot 5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 5-1\cdot 4}{5\cdot 5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>A.</alert>
By the product rule, 
<m>G'(3) = F'(3)\cdot H(3) + F(3)\cdot H'(3)
          = 2\cdot 5 + 1\cdot 4 = 14</m>.




<alert>B.</alert>
By the quotient rule,
<me>G'(3) = \frac{F'(3)\cdot H(3) - F(3)\cdot H'(3)}
                 {H(3)^2} 
          = \frac{2\cdot 5 - 1\cdot 4}{5^2} \approx 0.24.</me>



</solution>
